# Rift Challenge Testing Rules

## General
Every significant business feature should include tests.

Tests should verify behavior, not implementation details.

## Backend priorities
Highest priority:
- authentication;
- authorization;
- challenge ownership;
- challenge creation;
- participant limits;
- SoloQ/DuoQ rules;
- challenge start time;
- refresh throttling;
- Riot parsing;
- match deduplication;
- LP/rank calculations.

## Refresh tests
Explicitly test:
- first refresh accepted;
- second refresh before 2 minutes rejected/throttled;
- refresh after 2 minutes accepted;
- two concurrent refresh requests cannot bypass the limit.

The exact concurrency strategy must be appropriate for the deployed architecture.

## Riot tests
Mock external Riot API calls.
Do not make production/network requests in unit tests.

## Frontend tests
Prioritize:
- authentication UI;
- challenge creation form;
- participant limits;
- not-started state;
- active challenge visualization;
- refresh countdown;
- error states.

## Regression
When fixing a bug:
1. reproduce it with a test;
2. fix it;
3. keep the regression test.
